            {
                "entry_id": "c343df95-1c1a-3357-9372-196f830cdf73",
                "word": "webjournal",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1dcecd42-9369-4f17-b26c-5ca14e64b1c9",
                        "entry_id": "c343df95-1c1a-3357-9372-196f830cdf73",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "webjournaux"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f3957c55-e088-3644-8f1a-5c41ce3b32fd",
                        "entry_id": "c343df95-1c1a-3357-9372-196f830cdf73",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Journal publié sur une page du web."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neologism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "67fed02b-578e-4bca-a038-003c20731e85",
                                "sense_id": "f3957c55-e088-3644-8f1a-5c41ce3b32fd",
                                "text": "Ils ne savent pas encore comment fabriquer un webjournal. Ils se doutent que l'avenir est là mais ils n'ont pas la solution pour sauver le papier tout en développant le Net. Alors, ils tergiversent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b534b854-cf9e-4d65-a351-db239e9e4556",
                                "sense_id": "f3957c55-e088-3644-8f1a-5c41ce3b32fd",
                                "text": "À Jeu Égal lutte pour l'égalité des droits et lutte contre les LGBT-phobies. L'association édite un webjournal mensuel, Messaje."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9da1b53b-0781-4825-b867-9afafee28f37",
                                "sense_id": "f3957c55-e088-3644-8f1a-5c41ce3b32fd",
                                "text": "Si la presse en parlait encore, c'était surtout celle vendue aux caisses des supermarchés (le totem du Diable ou la trompette finale de la Bible) et les innombrables webjournaux dont une des chroniques se consacrait à la théorie du complot."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6c35e77-d831-4cfa-b87e-491188c82640",
                        "source_entry_id": "c343df95-1c1a-3357-9372-196f830cdf73",
                        "source_sense_id": "f3957c55-e088-3644-8f1a-5c41ce3b32fd",
                        "target_lang_word": "weblog",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "weblog",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db5782b9-47e3-3f0b-86f6-a16dd023d94e",
                                        "entry_id": "b6246238-008c-39c9-ba0a-f599be01af3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A website in the form of an ongoing journal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6155b50a-f52b-486f-993b-ebeab7432cc4",
                                                "sense_id": "db5782b9-47e3-3f0b-86f6-a16dd023d94e",
                                                "text": "A Weblog is updated as often as the writer decides and can include photographs and links to other sites around the Web. There are different ways to create a Weblog, and you do not need your own file server."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecb156d3-1ec7-467d-890e-be358f3d6fbf",
                                                "sense_id": "db5782b9-47e3-3f0b-86f6-a16dd023d94e",
                                                "text": "The case of the Loufan landslide indicates how a mainstream journalist-blogger used his weblog to expose the cover-up of an accident in north-west China."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a04f55fc-7567-4c6f-ae80-815902b48978",
                        "source_entry_id": "c343df95-1c1a-3357-9372-196f830cdf73",
                        "source_sense_id": "f3957c55-e088-3644-8f1a-5c41ce3b32fd",
                        "target_lang_word": "blog",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "blog",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfe252e9-5785-3686-9fbd-ed24f4dc75e3",
                                        "entry_id": "4a9a1503-2443-3f16-bb75-8a8b732e399b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A website that allows users to reflect, share opinions, and discuss various topics in the form of an online journal, sometimes letting readers comment on their posts. Most blogs are written in a slightly informal tone (personal journals, news, businesses, etc.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee8eef75-b274-4abd-a1ec-8180dbe1b4ed",
                                                "sense_id": "cfe252e9-5785-3686-9fbd-ed24f4dc75e3",
                                                "text": "So you see, the blog has been around since the beginning of the web; that is how basic the concept is. Today's blogs, and the activity of blogging, have taken on more meaning, but the concept of it all is still very simple and rooted in the beginning and intentions of the web itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f373b4a8-a264-48a8-b557-c85a0fba4759",
                                                "sense_id": "cfe252e9-5785-3686-9fbd-ed24f4dc75e3",
                                                "text": "Have you tried these, darling? They’re tempura zucchini flowers. Japanese-Italian fusion! My own invention. Shall I photograph it? We can put it on our blog."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9af4165e-7e53-39c8-a4a4-53041c434c63",
                                        "entry_id": "4a9a1503-2443-3f16-bb75-8a8b732e399b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An individual post to a blog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09890627-219e-4432-8d46-d28fdce70bd6",
                                                "sense_id": "9af4165e-7e53-39c8-a4a4-53041c434c63",
                                                "text": "This blog was originally posted on my personal site but is reproduced on the forums for greater visibility."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "blog",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3f2ac00-c453-3242-94af-79878b0286e4",
                                        "entry_id": "cca31637-a902-3c15-b87e-5785a87ead44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To contribute to a blog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet",
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d479cf7b-1993-4552-b881-40d48afe94d6",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f2ac00-c453-3242-94af-79878b0286e4",
                                                "text": "Blogger Anil Dash summed up the initial reaction well when he blogged his assessment of Macromedia's new blogging strategy: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d28d044-a600-49af-9317-64455688b50a",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f2ac00-c453-3242-94af-79878b0286e4",
                                                "text": "I hadn’t blogged myself, because I thought I had nothing to say. After 9/11, I did. So I planned to write the blog for a few weeks, until I ran out of memories."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "blog",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16c7afcd-6601-34e5-bf5a-07382785e889",
                                        "entry_id": "1ec776e1-425d-37ca-b184-11fc7b1af1fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To blag, to steal something; to acquire something illegally."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "blog",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b76cd752-bc3f-381d-9cfb-ec0a4b56f876",
                                        "entry_id": "ec46e6df-ee57-3203-84cb-fd4b5240476d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of Blog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "dated",
                                            "humorous",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d4b237d-d20c-4a10-bb85-6cf9d8fc5518",
                                                "sense_id": "b76cd752-bc3f-381d-9cfb-ec0a4b56f876",
                                                "text": "The earliest form we know about composed before Rhysling was blinded, at some drinking bout, and the verses concerned what he would do at the SoLaCon I—if he could find enough blog, a mimeo, and a few willing femmefans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80fc60a1-5332-4547-9030-ac937c94f868",
                                                "sense_id": "b76cd752-bc3f-381d-9cfb-ec0a4b56f876",
                                                "text": "The closest we came to that was not serving alcohol in the consuite one year. That was a significant success for it's [sic] main purpose. We actually came up with a definition of a fan, albeit a partial one phrased in the negative: Anyone who comes to Minicon just because there's free beer in the consuite is not a fan. That year there was more alcohol and more kinds* of alcohol than at any Minicon before or since; all the real fans who liked to drink brought their own and shared. The policy mainly discouraged the jerks who liked to hang out at the consuite and hit on the women. We did that for one year and happily went back to serving beer and blog."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1024af4c-7659-404e-b57e-342f0e28a2fa",
                                                "sense_id": "b76cd752-bc3f-381d-9cfb-ec0a4b56f876",
                                                "text": "I can't speak for Faye as ed of FHAPA, but it would be really swell of someone could send us a set of Intersection daily newszines, plus any con flyers or other fannish papers that were there to had for the picking up: fannish things, you know, not including media, gaming, filking or costuming, fine fun but not my cup of blog, thank you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
